.claude/workflows/ export-ignore
# The task-pack folder is a MIXED surface since 2026-09-21: the forward ledger
# (task-packs/FORWARD_LEDGER.md), its probes file, the router (CLAUDE.md) and the
# packs directly under task-packs/ and task-packs/Deferred/ are tracked and ship
# in every archive. The landed, merged and scrapped packs and the dated archive
# files stay untracked (gitignored, carried on the record branch), and these rows
# are a second wall for the NAMED subtrees and families only: git offers no
# re-include inside a pruned directory, so the folder cannot be walled wholesale
# once part of it ships, and a force-added stray outside these rows WOULD reach
# `git archive`. The catch-all is derived, not spelled: tests/test_surface_contract.py
# binds every tracked path under task-packs/ to the ship set, and
# tests/test_git_archive_parity.py binds every local-only-classified tracked
# path to archive absence. Parity twin for the bespoke release zip:
# surface_contract's `task-packs/` local-only prefix with its carve-out.
#
# The LEADING SLASH is load-bearing. Without it git matches the directory name at
# ANY depth, so a bare `task-packs/` rule (the one these replaced) also pruned
# espalier/assets/task-packs/CLAUDE.md — a packaged asset `espalier init` deploys —
# and a Download-ZIP init died mid-deploy with a bare Errno 2. Anchored, each row
# prunes its own top-level subtree or family only.
/task-packs/Done/ export-ignore
/task-packs/Merged/ export-ignore
/task-packs/Scrapped/ export-ignore
/task-packs/FORWARD_LEDGER_PRE_REBUILD_*.md export-ignore
/task-packs/ARCHIVE_*.md export-ignore
/task-packs/CONSOLIDATED_REGISTER_*.md export-ignore
/task-packs/RUNBOOK_*.md export-ignore
# TP-456 is the M4 release-console pack (operator console notes, not product); withheld from
